Link winpthreads by default on aarch64-w64-mingw32 posix-threads builds

For x86 targets configured with --enable-threads=posix, config.gcc adds
i386/mingw-pthread.h (a one-line, arch-neutral TARGET_USE_PTHREAD_BY_DEFAULT
define) to tm_file, which flips mingw/mingw32.h's LIB_SPEC from
"%{pthread:-lpthread}" to linking -lpthread by default (opt out with
-no-pthread). The new aarch64-*-mingw* stanza sets thread_file='posix' but
never adds that header, so plain "aarch64-w64-mingw32-g++ hello.cc" dies at
link with undefined pthread_* references -- libstdc++ and libgcc's
unwind-sjlj both depend on winpthreads in a posix-threads build. Mirror the
x86 conditional in the aarch64 stanza. No-op for x86 and for win32-threads
builds.

diff --git a/gcc/config.gcc b/gcc/config.gcc
index 7434217..c7d1c73 100644
--- a/gcc/config.gcc
+++ b/gcc/config.gcc
@@ -1325,6 +1325,9 @@ aarch64-*-mingw*)
 	tm_file="${tm_file} aarch64/aarch64-abi-ms.h"
 	tm_file="${tm_file} aarch64/aarch64-coff.h"
 	tm_file="${tm_file} aarch64/cygming.h"
+	if test x$enable_threads = xposix ; then
+		tm_file="${tm_file} i386/mingw-pthread.h"
+	fi
 	tm_file="${tm_file} mingw/mingw32.h"
 	tm_file="${tm_file} mingw/mingw-stdint.h"
 	tm_file="${tm_file} mingw/winnt.h"
